    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "interesting. you're saying we should actually move *away* from diversity in leadership to maintain stability? that seems counter-intuitive to most modern ESG standards. can you explain why you think an ethnically cohesive team would be more \"loyal\" or less prone to power struggles in an African context specifically? is there a pattern you're seeing in the data where diversity directly correlates to corporate instability in these emerging markets?",
